title    Seven Eighths Fusion (trio 7 feel)
composer Claude
about    The same 4-bar loop over Dm11, Bbmaj13#11, Gm9 and an altered A7, regrooved from a straight fusion backbeat into a swung jazz trio 7 feel with walking bass, ride cymbal, and pushed comping.

# Revision for the note "fusion 7 feels lame. keep everything, just make the
# groove like mehldau all the things we are 7 feel".
#
# How the note is read: Mehldau's "All the Things You Are" in 7 is a swinging
# trio groove, not a fusion groove. The pulse is seven walking quarter notes
# with swung eighths on a ride cymbal, the bar is felt in long and short
# groups, and the band pushes chord changes ahead of the beat together.
# "Keep everything" is read as: keep the harmony, voicings, instruments, bar
# length, tempo number, and the 2+2+3 phrasing, and change only the groove.
#
# What changed and why:
# - Same tempo and grid (tempo 240, beats 7, steps 2), so every bar lasts
#   exactly as long as before. The seven 240-bpm beats are now treated as the
#   walking pulse, and each beat splits into two swung eighths. swing 0.25 is
#   moderate, because swing flattens at a fast pulse.
# - Bass: root-fifth fusion figures become a walking line, one note per beat,
#   with chord tones on the group starts (beats 1, 3, 5) and chromatic
#   approaches into each next root.
# - Drums: the hi-hat sixteenths and snare backbeat are gone. A ride cymbal
#   plays a swung "ding ding-a" pattern bent to 2+2+3, with accents on the
#   three group starts so the phrasing stays audible. The hat plays only the
#   second beat of each group, like a hi-hat foot. The kick is feathered
#   quietly, and the snare plays sparse, different comping ghosts in each bar
#   instead of a repeated part.
# - Keys: identical voicings, but the on-grid stabs on every group start
#   become sparse, varied comping on swung offbeats, leaving beat 1 to the
#   bass more often.
# - Bar 4: the whole band pushes the altered A7 one swung eighth early (step 7
#   instead of step 8), the pad moves with it, and the snare and kick catch
#   the push. This anticipation is the most trio-like gesture in the loop.
# - Instruments are unchanged (epiano, strings, ebass) because the note says
#   to keep everything. The ride voice replaces the hat as timekeeper.
tempo    240
beats    7
steps    2
swing    0.25

# Electric piano: same rootless voicings as the original, now comped sparsely.
voice keys epiano vol=0.75 pan=-0.25
# String pad: unchanged common tones (E5+A5), moving to F5+Bb5 on A7alt.
voice pad strings vol=0.35 pan=0.3
# Fingered electric bass, slightly detached so the walking quarters articulate.
voice bass ebass vol=0.95 gate=0.85
voice kick kick vol=0.55
voice snare snare vol=0.6
voice ride ride vol=0.7
voice hat hat vol=0.4
voice crash crash vol=0.5

pattern A
# Keys comp, steps marked as (step, length).
# Bar 1 Dm11: (1,2) (7,3) (11,1), off the beat, leaving the downbeat to bass.
# Bar 2 Bbmaj13#11: (0,1) (3,2) (8,1) (10,4), held through the 3-group.
# Bar 3 Gm9: (3,2) (6,1) (9,3).
# Bar 4: Gm9 at (1,2), then A7alt pushed to step 7 and held to the loop point,
# where it resolves by half steps into Dm11 as before.
keys | . F3+C4+E4+G4+A4- .... F3+C4+E4+G4+A4-- . F3+C4+E4+G4+A4 .. | A3+D4+E4+G4 .. A3+D4+E4+G4- ... A3+D4+E4+G4 . A3+D4+E4+G4--- | .-- Bb3+D4+F4+A4- . Bb3+D4+F4+A4 .. Bb3+D4+F4+A4-- .. | . Bb3+D4+F4+A4- .... G3+C#4+F4+Bb4+C5------! |
# Pad: tied common tones, now moving at step 7 with the bar-4 push.
pad  | E5+A5------------- | -------------- | -------------- | ------- F5+Bb5------ |
# Bass walk, one note per beat (two steps):
# Bar 1 D E F G A C B, descending chromatically into Bb.
# Bar 2 Bb C D E F A Ab, descending chromatically into G.
# Bar 3 G F D C Bb A Ab, descending into G again.
# Bar 4 G Bb D, a short C on beat 4, A pushed to step 7 with the band, then
# E and C# approaching the D at the loop point.
bass | D2- E2- F2- G2- A2- C2- B1- | Bb1- C2- D2- E2- F2- A1- Ab1- | G2- F2- D2- C2- Bb1- A1- Ab1- | G1- Bb1- D2- C2 A1--! E2- C#2- |
# Ride: swung "ding ding-a" in 2+2+3, accents on the group starts (0, 4, 8)
# and a skip note on step 13 that leans into the next downbeat.
# Bar 4 drops the step-8 accent and hits step 7 instead, with the push.
ride  | X.xx X.xx X.x.xx | % | % | X.xx x.xX ..x.xx |
# Hat foot on the second beat of each group (steps 2, 6, 10).
hat   | ..x. ..x. ..x... | % | % | % |
# Kick feathered on group starts, with an accent on the bar-4 push.
kick  | o... o... o..... | % | % | o... o..X ...... |
# Snare comping: different ghosts in each bar, on swung offbeats.
snare | .... ...o ...x.. | ...o .... .o...x | .o.. ..o. ...o.. | ...o ...X ...o.x |
crash | X... .... ...... | _ | _ | _ |

loop A
